  "term": "imagery",
  "definition": "Imagery is a therapeutic exercise in which a practitioner uses calming, positive verbal images to help a person enter a semi-hypnotic state. It is used as a distraction and attention-based method in problems such as pain, hyperventilation, panic, and related conditions.",
